  "tagline": "Open-source backend platform on Postgres with Hasura GraphQL, auth, storage and functions.",
  "description": "Nhost is an open-source backend platform that gives each project a dedicated PostgreSQL database exposed through the Hasura GraphQL Engine (queries, mutations, realtime subscriptions and event triggers with role-based permissions), plus authentication, file storage with image transformation, serverless functions and an AI toolkit with pgvector. It can be self-hosted with Docker or used as Nhost Cloud. It is a natural Firebase alternative for teams that want GraphQL and plain Postgres underneath rather than a proprietary document store.",
